    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0072" n="60" xml:id="pg60"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/607: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-26T21:00:00+04:00">June 26, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 26—4:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. The Legation has just been informed by New Delhi of the violation of Afghan
                    territory yesterday by an American aircraft. Because of the seriousness with
                    which the Afghan Government might view the incident and because of long delay in
                    receipt of telegrams from Department the Legation without awaiting instructions
                    is expressing regrets on behalf of the American Government to the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d60-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thayer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d60-f1" n="23" xml:id="d60-f1-content">
                <p>All Mohammed Khan.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
